    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "$ABCD$ is a rectangle. The coordinates of $A$, $B$ and $C$ are $(1,-6)$, $(1,2)$ and $(7,2)$. What are the coordinates of $D$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$D(7,-6)$",
      "worked": "$AB$ is vertical and $BC$ is horizontal. The opposite sides of the rectangle are parallel, so $D$ has the same horizontal coordinate as $C$ and the same vertical coordinate as $A$.\n\nTherefore $D=(7,-6)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
